---
name: review-issue
description: "Verify whether an issue is resolved by comparing its requirements with code and fresh check results. Use for resolution review of GitHub or local issues. Return a report; comment or close only when requested. Not for pre-implementation analysis or general PR review."
license: MIT
compatibility: Requires a coding agent with filesystem access; Node.js 22.13+ for bundled helpers, Git for repository operations, and authenticated GitHub access only for remote work.
---

# Review Issue

Use this Skill only for its requested responsibility. Work in the consumer project, honoring its instructions and existing authorization. Resource links below belong to this installed Skill; project inputs and outputs belong to the consumer repository.

## Workflow

1. Identify the requested input, scope and output; read [issue input](references/issue-input.md) when resolving a demand or artifact location.
2. For repository-dependent decisions, read [repository policy](references/repository-policy.md).
3. Follow [review-issue](references/review-issue.md), loading the resources below when that procedure needs them.
4. Return the requested artifact or evidence-based result; report material blockers without expanding the task.

## Resources to load when needed

- Only when an installed CLI can enrich policy/scaffold decisions: [cli-integration](references/cli-integration.md).
- Before implementing, reviewing or claiming completion: [evidence](references/evidence.md).
- When returning an issue review: [issue-review-result](references/issue-review-result.md).
- Before a remote mutation: [publication](references/publication.md).

## Bundled helpers

Paths in commands are relative to this Skill root. Execute by absolute resolved path while keeping the consumer project as the working directory. Run a helper with `--help` first. No helper installs the Issue Flow CLI.

- [scripts/optional-cli.mjs](scripts/optional-cli.mjs)
